# .dockerignore — F-07 (0.33.0): production image hygiene.
# Without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile baked into the image:
#   - the LIVE engagement database `webpent.db` (+ its WAL/SHM siblings)
#   - 36MB of docs/, 4.8MB of reports/ (engagement evidence), 5.7MB of tests/
#   - caches, virtualenvs and local-only artifacts
# Image layers are extractable by anyone with registry access — engagement
# data must never travel inside them.

# --- Engagement data / state ---
webpent.db
webpent.db-wal
webpent.db-shm
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
output/
memory/
evidence/
reports/

# --- Non-runtime trees ---
docs/
tests/
scripts/
benchmark/
ground_truth/
lab/
profiles/
templates/

# --- VCS and local config ---
.git/
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Python build/cache noise ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- Virtualenvs ---
.venv/
venv/

# --- Editor / OS ---
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
